 "final_required_human_decision": "Two questions require a human ruling. They are independent.\n\nQ1 \u2014 Are the three deviations Inspector B classified as TRUE_STRUCTURAL_DEFECT actually defects, or correct geometry at the resolution limit? All three are real and measured: neck inset 7.3 px vs 8.0 px reference (0.7 px shallow), shoulder peak 1.44 px at row 706, flare/collar seam 1.84 px at row 495. All three sit far inside every deterministic gate (largest is 0.0076 normalized against a 0.035 limit), and the reference itself is quantized to +/-0.5 px. Inspector A saw the same evidence and classified all of them as presentation artifacts. The automated layer cannot break this tie: it is a judgment about what 'faithful' means at sub-2-pixel scale.\n\nQ2 \u2014 Should the GLASS contour be re-fitted? Its adaptive 0.6 px tolerance was never enforced because the chain exceeded the fitter's segment budget and fell into uniform chunking. Re-fitting would change M3 geometry, which this mandate prohibits, so it was disclosed rather than done. A re-fit would likely reduce the shoulder and seam deviations. It would also mean a new candidate and a new inspection cycle.\n\nNo further geometry candidate may be generated until you rule. M3S1 and M3S2 remain prohibited.",
